{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360430-question-about-leviathan-the-tempest","id":1360430,"title":"Question about Leviathan: the Tempest?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-11T19:46:43-08:00","id":1360430,"title":"Question about Leviathan: the Tempest?","content":"How do Leviathans interact with the Makara from Beast? Just a hypo question since I\u2019m probably never gonna play either of these creatures (I tried reading Beast and it creeped me out for some reason), but I\u2019m stuck at home bored and I wanted to see what people would say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T08:51:35-08:00","id":1360524,"title":"","content":"I'm tired, don't particularly actually want to read Leviathan right now due to <i>reasons</i>, and actually have some reasons I'm gonna keep my Makara readings that are probably relevant close to the chest, soooooo enjoy this post from ages ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/765301-begotten-and-wicked-children-of-the-dark-mother?p=765648#post765648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leviathan's main point of distinction lies in that the monsters they are tend to be focused on cataclysm-these things destroy towns at the low end and end worlds on the high, and so reining them in is a big deal. Beasts are inclined to look at the closeness of them and might declare the first group to branch off, when mankind started becoming advanced enough to worry not just about their own death, but the death of the species. Nightmares of Extinction, if you will.<br /> <br /> They might consider them kin, but Leviathans put Beasts in a weird spot. Beasts are very much about accepting their monstrous state, embracing it and living it up. If Leviathans do that though, it invites calamity on a scale even Ravagars might not be comfortable with. Leviathans are the fragile or disabled kids in the family tree, and the Beast, bursting with energy and a need of play, just don't know quite what to do with them. They want to help, but it's apparent that they might make things worse from the word go.<br /> <br /> That's the best reading I can offer, anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Begotten and Wicked: Children of the Dark Mother, Beast: The Primordial subform, if you want to see a fuller discussion about it, though warning, there's a dumb argument made in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-12-2020, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T09:22:17-08:00","id":1360532,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> cool. In Enemy Action there\u2019s a reference to leviathans in the writeup for the exile Damocles. (I may seem a little flaky but I\u2019m actually really good at reading stuff closely.) Is that just an Easter egg or are they thinking about making Leviathan a legit game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T10:17:36-08:00","id":1360546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1360430-question-about-leviathan-the-tempest?p=1360532#post1360532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that just an Easter egg or are they thinking about making Leviathan a legit game?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Leviathan&quot; is a normal word that does not necessarily refer to anything more specific than &quot;a sea monster,&quot; which is part of why the Makara have it as a nickname.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i